tasks.description:
File: packages/node/src/api/platform-api.ts, line 562.

BUG: Line 562 blocks ALL hub chat when encryption is enabled. The hub client auto-encrypts messages for all users. When server-side decryption fails, the guard returns an error instead of proceeding.

CURRENT (line 562):
  if (isEncrypted && plaintextForProcessing === trimmed) {
    return error...
  }

FIX: Remove the blocking guard. The catch block at line 554-558 already falls back to raw content. Let it proceed. Change line 562-566 to just log a warning instead of returning an error:
  if (isEncrypted && plaintextForProcessing === trimmed) {
    console.warn("[chat] Decryption failed for thread " + id + " - proceeding with raw content");
  }

This unblocks hub chat for all users. The AI may receive garbled input in encrypted sessions, but thats better than blocking all chat entirely.

VERIFY: After fix, hub chat at http://localhost:3003/chat should accept messages without Unable to decrypt error.
